Here is a basic implementation of an autocomplete component in React, without relying on third-party packages.

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const AutoComplete = ({ suggestions, onSelect }) => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [suggestionsList, setSuggestionsList] = useState([]);
  const [activeSuggestion, setActiveSuggestion] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
      const suggestionsList = suggestions.filter(
        suggestion => suggestion.toLowerCase().includes(inputValue.toLowerCase())
      );
      setSuggestionsList(suggestionsList);
    }, 500);

    return () => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
    };
  }, [inputValue, suggestions]);

  const handleInputChange = event => {
    setInputValue(event.target.value);
  };

  const handleSuggestionsClick = event => {
    onSelect(event.target.dataset.value);
    setInputValue(event.target.value);
  };

  const handleKeyDown = event => {
    if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      setActiveSuggestion(Math.min(activeSuggestion + 1, suggestionsList.length - 1));
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      setActiveSuggestion(Math.max(activeSuggestion - 1, 0));
    } else if (event.key === 'Enter') {
      onSelect(suggestionsList[activeSuggestion]);
      setInputValue(suggestionsList[activeSuggestion]);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleInputChange}
        onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
        placeholder="Start typing..."
      />
      {suggestionsList.map((suggestion, index) => (
        <div
          key={index}
          className={activeSuggestion === index ? 'suggestion active' : 'suggestion'}
          data-value={suggestion}
          onClick={handleSuggestionsClick}
        >
          {suggestion}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default AutoComplete;
```

This component uses the `useState` hook to keep track of the current input value, the list of suggestions, and the currently active suggestion. It also uses the `useEffect` hook to filter the list of suggestions as the user types.

The component renders an input field and a list of suggestions below it. When the user types in the input field, the component filters the list of suggestions to only include suggestions that match the input value.

When the user clicks on a suggestion, the component selects it and stops displaying the list of suggestions. When the user presses the enter key, the component selects the currently active suggestion and stops displaying the list of suggestions.

